==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing F_PermissionMatrix leaves PermMatrix.Allowed unconstrained; the injection forces a forbidden cell (ComplianceReviewer → ClaimApplication) into the Allowed set, which LeastPrivilege and FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly must detect.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_002_CustomerPermissions, FR_003_LoanOfficerPermissions, FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly, FR_023_ComplianceWriteDenied, PermissionGrounding
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_002_CustomerPermissions: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_003_LoanOfficerPermissions: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_ComplianceReviewerReadOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_023_ComplianceWriteDenied: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionGrounding: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecidedByAssignedOfficer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecidedByAssignedOfficer.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the constraint that the deciding officer must be the assigned officer. The injection forces a Decision whose decidedBy differs from the application's assignedOfficer, directly violating FR_013_AssignedOfficerDecides.
    expected to FAIL: FR_013_AssignedOfficerDecides
      - FR_013_AssignedOfficerDecides: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneInFlightPerCustomer  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AtMostOneInFlightPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the in-flight uniqueness constraint. The injection forces a single customer to own two Submitted applications simultaneously, violating FR-008.
    expected to FAIL: FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer
      - FR_008_OneInFlightPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ExactlyOneInitialAuditEntry  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_ExactlyOneInitialAuditEntry.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the requirement that every application has exactly one submission audit entry. The injection forces an application to have no initial audit entry, violating AuditCompleteness and FR_009_SubmissionAuditEntry.
    expected to FAIL: FR_009_SubmissionAuditEntry, AuditCompleteness, FR_019_ExactlyOneAuditPerTransition
      - FR_009_SubmissionAuditEntry: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_019_ExactlyOneAuditPerTransition: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionExistsIffDecided  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_DecisionExistsIffDecided.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the coupling between decision records and application status. The injection forces an Approved application to have no associated Decision, violating the atomicity invariant in FR_015_AtomicDecision.
    expected to FAIL: FR_015_AtomicDecision
      - FR_015_AtomicDecision: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditValidTransitions  → runs/A-L2/mutated_F_AuditValidTransitions.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact removes the restriction on which (previous, new) status pairs are valid in audit events. The injection forces an audit entry with previousStatus=Approved (a terminal state), violating FR_016_DecidedImmutability's assertion that no event departs from a decided status.
    expected to FAIL: FR_016_DecidedImmutability, AppendOnly
      - FR_016_DecidedImmutability: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

